# ---- agent-call choke point: the prompt ledger (BH-1037) -------------------
# bin/agent-call.sh looks up a persisted row keyed (project, stage, promptsha)
# BEFORE the first runner is invoked, and inside the TTL replays a recorded
# ok/empty answer instead of buying it again. One line per replay in
# logs/agent-call-ledger.log; the rows live under
# state/agent-call-ledger/<project>/<stage>/<promptsha>.{json,out} and are swept
# once an hour at 2x the TTL. Every value below is the code's REAL default.
#
# OPT-IN, PER CALLER. 0 (the default) = no read and no write, i.e. the ladder
# exactly as it was before BH-1037. The one caller that turns it on does so on
# its own call: mc_rereview exports AGENT_CALL_LEDGER=1 because its prompt
# carries the head sha and that head's diff, and its deliverable IS the text it
# reads back. The other stage-`review` callers (run-build's review lenses,
# review-rescue) must NOT replay: their prompt names no head, and their
# deliverable is the review.md file the agentic session writes. Setting this to
# 1 box-wide turns the ledger on for those too — don't, unless you mean it.
# `flags/agent-call-ledger-off` disables it even where a caller set it.
#AGENT_CALL_LEDGER=0
# How long a recorded answer may be replayed for, in seconds. Non-numeric falls
# back to 1800 rather than making the comparison false forever.
#AGENT_CALL_LEDGER_TTL_S=1800
# Which stages an OPTED-IN caller may read AND write, space or comma separated
# (`*` = all). Default `review` on purpose: these are AGENTIC sessions, so
# replaying an `execute` would return the transcript while performing none of
# the edits. This narrows the opt-in above; it never grants it.
#AGENT_CALL_LEDGER_STAGES=review
# Which runners the failover ladder may call, space or comma separated (BH-1019,
# not part of the ledger above). Unset (the default) = today's ladder,
# untouched. Set, and a rung whose runner is not named is skipped; an allowed
# primary that is not installed/authed is REFUSED with rc 2 and
# AGENT_CALL_REFUSED as the first line of the outfile, before anything is
# bought. Normally set per CALL (bin/lib/merge-conductor-lib.sh's re-review
# passes AGENT_CALL_RUNNERS=claude, because it rejects a non-Claude read anyway;
# MC_RR_RUNNERS is the operator's way back) rather than box-wide.
#AGENT_CALL_RUNNERS=

